  annotation = {中文辅助译名：月球地震探测任务模拟：波场建模、MEMS 地震仪和阵列优化},
  abstract = {Lunar seismic exploration is a crucial approach for revealing the internal structure and geological evolution of the Moon. The seismic network deployed during the Apollo missions recorded numerous lunar seismic events, laying the foundation for lunar science. However, due to the sparse station distribution, limited instrument bandwidth, and poor signal coherence, the detection capability for weak events and shallow fine structures was significantly constrained. With the advancement of China’s Phase IV Lunar Exploration Program and the International Lunar Research Station (ILRS), an urgent challenge is how to efficiently evaluate scientific mission schemes prior to implementation. To address this issue, this paper proposes a fullchain simulation framework covering the entire process of “source-propagation-observation,” including wavefield modeling, instrument modeling, and array optimization. In wavefield modeling, a hybrid finite-difference time-domain (FDTD)-finite element method (FEM) is employed, incorporating a Q-value viscoelastic model and convolutional perfectly matched layer (CPML) absorbing boundary conditions to accurately reproduce the high-frequency attenuation and long-tail effects observed in Apollo data. For instrument modeling, a system-level MEMS lunar seismometer model is constructed, taking into account thermal noise, circuit noise, and feedback noise. Quantitative calculations are performed for the input signal, noise signal, and system output response. Fo},
}

